{"title":"1992 OIM Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368b6f971b418d731c62ff2cb59f51c527d22849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is constructed as shown in the figure. \n</p><p>Show that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e404f0e7cc3851c1dfea4d938a092dbdf78e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[area(H) \\ge 13.area(T)\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Ibe7_2.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8b/Ibe7_2.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"203\" height=\"146\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For this problem were going to denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as the area of hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>We know that the area of an isosceles triangle is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c0226803a11576578b2b94ef8051fced876e7682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2sin(\\theta)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the length of the sides that are equal and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle between them. \n</p><p>We notice that there are 6 isosceles triangles in the hexagon with three of them sharing the area of the inside triangle in common  Therefore we can write an equation for the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by adding all of those triangles and then subtracting 2 times the area of the triangle:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67acf6500dfd9672c1c80275d23246d7da5eec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H=\\frac{a^2sin(A)}{2}+\\frac{b^2sin(B)}{2}+\\frac{c^2sin(C)}{2}+\\frac{(a+b)^2sin(C)}{2}+\\frac{(a+c)^2sin(B)}{2}+\\frac{(b+c)^2sin(A)}{2}-2T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"776\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1bf54e26a89cb78426f4249f1533579fa7b68c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H=(a^2+b^2+c^2)(sin(A)+sin(B)+sin(C))+(2ab.sin(C)+2ac.sin(B)+2bc.sin(A))-4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"759\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Using the extended law of sines:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/15933748a4e0138184e3275ac26cc22356b2ffcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(A)=\\frac{a}{2R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"34\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fc5b33da2abd08c67dd68e440a09bdaa13c74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(B)=\\frac{b}{2R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9acaad1db85d5dc0f9798999a05ef34ec9c63d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin(C)=\\frac{c}{2R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumradius of the triangle\n</p><p>Substitute into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af404afdcd6227f71e6ebc384ecf5826a8bf1c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b3472b61d410066b02b6ea1fc6172bf1e926c6bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H=(a^2+b^2+c^2)\\left( \\frac{a}{2R}+\\frac{b}{2R}+\\frac{c}{2R} \\right)+\\left(2ab\\frac{c}{2R}+2ac\\frac{b}{2R}+2bc\\frac{a}{2R}\\right)-4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"609\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e485ddda8beade8a4760060ba13afd02e8691e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H=\\left( \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{2R} \\right)+\\left(2ab\\frac{c}{2R}+2ac\\frac{b}{2R}+2bc\\frac{a}{2R}\\right)-4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"568\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d509cf98f4c402a40c8beeeb2b4bdec10e69ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2H= \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{2R} +\\frac{3abc}{R}-4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"351\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1d25a9051c47167760733637ef447edcf6623b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H= \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R} +\\frac{3abc}{2R}-2T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"342\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Also from the extended law of sines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/052e3c2a6dfe1f92f398e97837707b6f61f5adfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=\\frac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"39\" /> therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1feb73458b94557ec6d33226abc6c5403ba145cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3abc}{2R}=6T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e00ad688a585cea8484cea4005c13ca188a8ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H= \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R} +4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"281\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Applying AM-GM:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53ebbc78f5de16153c9aebc06b6b57f3cbd20e90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{9}=\\frac{a^3+b^3+c^3+ac^2+ab^2+ba^2+bc^2+ca^2+cb^2}{9} \\ge \\sqrt[9]{a^9b^9c^9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"683\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0ab73d90e82c97ff17ad15a4562ee4b0bf022cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{9} \\ge abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"245\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57cac4d5a61c499e42d375d5777f6da11b667e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c) \\ge 9abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e13296f67786c398137112442d66d185efe975a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R} \\ge 9\\frac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"258\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35ba1681d998865f850125e13fb830d2d44d6169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R} \\ge 9T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d036ba1fbe2283ad63d160b87c9639af45c58f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R}+4T \\ge 9T+4T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"331\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc7037df36e11583983907c428bcb6cf2c7c19d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H \\ge 13T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, which proves: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d996ef9c7f30ecb7c3067565d5dc180865eae80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$area(H) \\ge 13.area(T)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Equality holds with equilateral triangle:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832fc7d916454c1738ba74fbe56ced7836328df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=\\frac{a^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae5e74266a54f6144fc529b1a9d573bc5686a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=\\frac{a}{2sin(A)}=\\frac{a}{2\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"218\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9ddaf9e70ac5f386857aabb82b3d52cb1f9a3cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H= \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)(a+b+c)}{4R} +4T=\\frac{(3a^2)(3a)}{4\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}} +4T=\\frac{9a\\sqrt{3}}{4}+4T=9T+4T=13T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"689\" height=\"52\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note.  I actually competed at this event in Venezuela when I was in High School representing Puerto Rico.  I think I got 1 or 2 points out of 10 on this one.  I don't remember what I did.</li></ul>\n<p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017180615\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 241/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8992/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.087      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    7.087      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26080:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017180615 and revision id 208214. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}